# ==============================================================================
# SECRETS — NEVER COMMIT
# ==============================================================================
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak
*.env.bak*

# Any SUFFIXED variant of ".env". The patterns above miss every one of them:
# ".env" matches that exact basename only, and "*.env" below matches basenames
# ENDING in ".env" — so ".env.hid" was ignored by neither. That is not a
# hypothetical name: CONTRIBUTING.md's own pre-push procedure is
# `mv .env .env.hid` ... `mv .env.hid .env`, and a run that stops before the
# restore leaves a full set of live secrets sitting untracked-but-committable,
# one `git add -A` from the history. Ignoring the whole suffix space is right
# because a suffixed .env is always a copy of a real one.
# Placed BEFORE the negations so the .example templates still win.
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/credentials.json

# Catch-all for env files whose basename does NOT start with ".env" —
# deploy.env, prod.env, staging.env. Every pattern above requires the basename
# to START with ".env", which is why space.env needed its own line further down,
# and why Caddyfile's own instructions ("put PUBLIC_API_DOMAIN in deploy.env")
# name a file that was not ignored at all.
*.env
!*.env.example


